sn55.27:8.4 | P: itipi so bhagavā …pe… satthā devamanussānaṁ buddho bhagavāti. | T: ‘Indeed, the Blessed One is worthy & rightly self-awakened, consummate in clear-knowing & conduct, well-gone, an expert with regard to the cosmos, unexcelled trainer of people fit to be tamed, teacher of devas & human beings, awakened, blessed.’
sn55.27:8.5 | S: Seeing in themselves that experiential confidence in the Buddha, they’re not frightened or terrified, and don’t fear what awaits them after death. | T: (none)
sn55.27:9.1 | S: Furthermore, a noble disciple has experiential confidence in the teaching … | T: “Further, the disciple of the noble ones is endowed with verified confidence in the Dhamma:
sn55.27:9.2 | P: svākkhāto bhagavatā dhammo …pe… paccattaṁ veditabbo viññūhīti. | T: ‘The Dhamma is well taught by the Blessed One, to be seen here & now, timeless, inviting verification, pertinent, to be experienced by the observant for themselves.’
sn55.27:9.3 | P: Tañca panassa dhamme aveccappasādaṁ attani samanupassato na hoti uttāso, na hoti chambhitattaṁ, na hoti samparāyikaṁ maraṇabhayaṁ. | T: (none)
sn55.27:10.1 | S: Furthermore, a noble disciple has experiential confidence in the Saṅgha … | T: “Further, the disciple of the noble ones is endowed with verified confidence in the Saṅgha:
